==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|l|u}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|urj-pro|fi}} {{recons|loŋe-|lang=urj-pro||to throw, push away}}[http://starling.rinet.ru/cgi-bin/etymology.cgi?single=1&basename=/data/uralic/uralet&text_number=+498&root=config].

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyphenation|luo|da}}
* {{rhymes|uodɑ|lang=fi}}
* {{IPA|lang=fi|/ˈluɔdɑ(ʔ)/}}

===Verb===
{{fi-verb}}

# {{transitive}} To [[create]].
# {{transitive}} ''luoda [[lumi|lunta]]'': To [[shovel]] [[snow]].
# {{transitive}} To [[shed]].
#: ''Lamppu '''luo''' sinistä valoa.''
#:: The lamp '''sheds''' a blue light.
# To [[exuviate]], [[slough]], [[molt]] (to shed or cast off a covering, especially a skin); used always with an object that reveals what is being exuviated.
#: ''Käärme alkoi '''luoda nahkaansa'''.''
#:: The snake began to '''exuviate''' its '''old skin'''.
#: ''Kun hummeri kasvaa, se '''luo kuorensa'''.''
#:: As it grows, a lobster will '''exuviate'''.

